{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-34618-r4535456","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Black Forest Cake","sourcePageId":34618,"sourceRevision":"4535456","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-09-03T10:17:34Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Dndnrmn1IsBack2025","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Black%20Forest%20Cake&oldid=4535456","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:24:43.580Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baking recipes","Category:Difficult recipes","Category:German recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for black forest cake","Category:Recipes for dessert","Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour","Category:Recipes using brandy","Category:Recipes using brewed coffee","Category:Recipes using brown sugar","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using cherry","Category:Recipes using dark chocolate","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using fruit preserves","Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon","Category:Recipes using self-raising flour","Category:Recipes using whipped cream","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"16f2eed3c7af89846f85d446d7b31af97a53798bc326d4812be553de584b11c0","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary|category=Cake recipes|yield=8 slices|time=3 hours|difficulty=4|image=[[File:Black Forest gateau.jpg|300px]]\n}}\n__NOTOC__\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Germany|German Cuisine]]\n\n'''Black Forest Cake''', sometimes called by the French ''gateau'', ''gateaux'' or ''gâteau'' (meaning \"cake\"), is a chocolate cake with a strong cherry element. The recipe originates from Germany, where it is called '''[[Cookbook:Schwarzwälder Kirschtorte|Schwarzwälder Kirschtorte]]'''.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n=== Cake ===\n* 4 oz (100 g) [[cookbook:butter|butter]]\n* 8 oz (225 g) [[cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n* 4 oz (100 g) plain [[cookbook:chocolate|chocolate]]\n* 7 oz (200 g) [[cookbook:Flour|self-raising flour]]\n* ¼ teaspoon ground [[cookbook:cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n* ¼ pint [[cookbook:Sour Cream|sour cream]]\n* 3 tablespoons strong cold black [[cookbook:coffee|coffee]]\n* 2 [[cookbook:egg|egg]]s\n* 1 pinch of [[cookbook:salt|salt]]\n\n=== Pastry base ===\n* 4 oz (100 g) [[cookbook:Flour|cream flour]]\n* 1 pinch of [[cookbook:salt|salt]]\n* 2 oz (50 g) [[cookbook:Powdered Sugar|icing sugar]]\n* 2 oz (50 g) Irish [[cookbook:butter|butter]]\n* 1 [[cookbook:Egg yolk|egg yolk]]\n* a few drops of [[Cookbook:Vanilla|vanilla essence]]\n\n=== Misc. ===\n* 1 pint [[cookbook:cream|cream]]\n* 1 tin (1 lb) black [[cookbook:cherry|cherries]]\n* 4 tablespoons black cherry jam\n* [[cookbook:brandy|brandy]] or cherry juice\n* 4 oz (100 g) grated [[cookbook:chocolate|chocolate]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n=== Cake ===\n# [[Cookbook:Creaming|Cream]] the butter and sugar together well.\n# Melt the chocolate and [[Cookbook:Beat|beat]] into the creamed mixture, then beat in the eggs.\n# Sift flour, salt and cinnamon together.\n# Fold the dry mix lightly into the liquids, then fold in the sour cream and cold coffee.\n# Pour the mixture into a lined and greased 9-inch round, deep [[Cookbook:Cake Pan|cake tin]], and bake for 1 hour and 25 minutes.\n# Set to cool on a wire rack.\n\n=== Pastry base ===\n# Mix all the ingredients together in a bowl and bind until the mixture stiffens.\n# Roll the pastry onto a floured board worktable until pastry is about the same size as the base of the cake tin.\n# Lay out on [[Cookbook:Baking Sheet|baking sheet]] and bake for 20–25 minutes at 350°F, or until a toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean.\n\n=== Assembly ===\n# [[Cookbook:Whipping|Whip]] cream until it holds its shape.\n# Put some whipped cream into pastry [[Cookbook:Pastry Bag|piping bag]] with a star tip attached, and reserve this for the decoration.\n# Slice the cake horizontally into 3 equal-sized layers.\n# Drain the cherries, reserve 8 for decoration and remove the stones from the remainder.\n# Put pastry on serving plate and spread the pastry with black cherry jam.\n# Soak the cakes with brandy or cherry juice.\n# Put one layer of cake on top of coated pastry.\n# Spread a layer of cream on the cake, and top with half the stoned cherries.\n# Add the second layer of cake, then another layer of cream and cherries.\n# Top with the final layer of the cake.\n# Cover the entire cake with the remaining cream, and press on the grated chocolate.\n# Decorate the top with piped rosettes of cream and the reserved whole black cherries.\n\n== Notes, tips and variations ==\n* Using 3 identical cake pans instead of 1 large one is acceptable.\n\n* Margarine, vegetable oil or regular butter will substitute for Irish butter.\n\n* In some countries (e.g. Austria and Australia) the brandy is often replaced by rum, in Germany itself it is almost always replaced by Kirschwasser.\n\n* Cakes usually work at between 325°F and 400°F (160°C and 205°C). Pastries usually work at between 350°F and 425°F (175°C and 220°C).\n\n== Similar recipes ==\n<categorytree mode=\"all\">Recipes for black forest cake</categorytree>\n[[Category:German recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Recipes for black forest cake]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cherry]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dark chocolate]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes with images]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Recipes using whipped cream]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brandy]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brewed coffee]]\n[[Category:Recipes using self-raising flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fruit preserves]]","isRecipe":false,"recipe":{"name":"Black Forest Cake","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[],"steps":[],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extraction only; no culinary/editorial review.","Ingredient quantities, units, alternatives, food identities, aggregate duration, and nutrition remain unknown until individually parsed/reviewed.","Source-level CC BY-SA policy applies generally; page-specific exceptions have not been checked."]}},"parsedRecipe":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"wikibooks:34618","recordId":"wikibooks-34618-r4535456","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceRevision":"4535456","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Black%20Forest%20Cake&oldid=4535456","sourceSha256":"16f2eed3c7af89846f85d446d7b31af97a53798bc326d4812be553de584b11c0","parserVersion":"wikibooks-sections-v3","quantityParserVersion":"source-prefix-v2","license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is